--TEST--
A stream `Core\Response::stream` started with `$mustEnd` and never ended is an error on standard error that names it and fails the run — `rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-writes-as-a-stream`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response::stream
// The program writes a part and returns without `end()`. Nothing catches the
// error: the program has already ended, so it is reported the way an uncaught
// throw is, after everything the program printed, and the run exits with 1.
var $body = Core\Response::stream("text/csv", null, null, "orders.csv");
$body->write("id,name\n");
--EXPECT--
id,name
--EXPECT-ERROR--
{"level":"error","msg":"A response stream started with `$mustEnd` was not ended, so its body is cut off. Call `end()` on the stream before the program ends.","fields":{"stream":"orders.csv"}}
